meta {
  name: Toggle player vest
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/practices/:practiceId/players/:playerId/vest
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  playerId: 22
  practiceId: 14
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("returns the team header fragment", function() {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.not.be.empty;
  });
}

docs {
  Flips the vest flag for one player and re-renders that team's header
  (the vest count). Run twice to toggle back.
  
  The player must already be in this practice — `playerId` alone isn't
  enough, it's the practice/player PAIR that has to exist.
  
  ## Edge cases
  
  | URL change | Expected |
  |---|---|
  | player `999999` | `500`, empty body |
  | a real player not in this practice | `500`, empty body |
  | `/practices/abc/players/xyz/vest` | `400`, empty body |
  
  Where the `500` comes from: `TogglePracticePlayerVest` uses
  `RETURNING team_number`, so a non-matching row gives `sql.ErrNoRows`,
  and the handler's error branch doesn't distinguish that from a real
  database failure.
}
